msgstr ""

#: ../../../project-security/verifying-signatures.rst:293
#: 134036f74aaf4515b30f0db59882d593
msgid ""
"This is just an example, so the output you receive may not look exactly the "
"same (:samp:`{X}` will be replaced by the release number). What matters is "
"the line with a ``sig!`` prefix showing that the QMSK has signed this key. "
"This verifies the authenticity of the RSK. Note that the ``!`` flag after "
"the ``sig`` tag is important because it means that the key signature is "
"valid. A ``sig-`` prefix would indicate a bad signature, and ``sig%`` would "
"mean that gpg encountered an error while verifying the signature. It is not "
"necessary to independently verify the authenticity of the RSK, since you "
"already verified the authenticity of the QMSK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../project-security/verifying-signatures.rst:295
#: b0fe22f9b39049abbe7fba7d367cf722
msgid ""
"As a final sanity check, make sure the RSK is in your keyring with the "
"correct trust level:"
msgstr ""

